  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">A) # of customized wetland management action plan with allocated budget plans developed/revised and are under implementation
B) Hectarage of fragile wetland ecosystems under the coverage of customized management plans under implementation)
C) # of monitoring stations equipped and operational
D) # of local communities benefiting from livelihood initiatives (gender-based) 
E) % of decrease in water and agrochemical usage in selected pilot sites 
F) # of new pilot villages in which climate smart practices have been implemented
G) # of CEPA centers which are established and functional 
H) # of wetland management initiative being implemented by the local community</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2021">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">A) 3 Management Plans developed but action plans with allocated budget needs to be developed 
B) 60,000 ha of Hectarage of fragile wetland ecosystems under the coverage of customized management plans 
C) 2 monitoring stations but not fully equipped and functional
D) 12,000 local farmers trained in previous pilot sites in LU basin
E) Average 30% decrease in water and agrochemical usage in previous pilot sites
F) 191 villages as previous pilot villages in which climate smart practices have been implemented
G) 3 wetlands information centers but no CEPA centers
H) Some wetland management local initiatives in the pilot sites</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">A) 3 Management Plans action plan developed/revised and are under implementation (1 action plan for each site)
B) At least 400,000 ha of fragile wetland ecosystems under the coverage of customized management plans (under implementation) (250,000 ha Lake Urmia, 100,000 ha Shadegan, 50,000 ha Bakhtegan)
C) 3 monitoring stations equipped and operational (1 in each wetland)
D) 1,098 local communities benefited from livelihood initiatives (1600 person in Lake Urmia basin and 400 person in each of Shadegan and Bakhtegan, out of which 50% of them are women) 
E) 30% of decrease in water and agrochemical usage in selected pilot sites
F) 98 new pilot villages in which climate smart practices have been implemented (77 pilots in Lake Urmia basin and 10 in Shadegan and 11 in Bakhtegan wetlands)
G) Procure the required equipment for operationalizing the Communication, Education, Public Awareness (CEPA) centers in the 3 pilot sits.
H) 3 wetland Management initiative being implemented by local community (1 in Lake Urmia basin and 1 in each of Shadegan and Bakhtegan wetlands</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">A) 7 Management Plans developed.
B) 554,632 ha of fragile wetland ecosystems under the coverage of customized management plans.
C) 3 monitoring stations equipped and operational.
D) 1,098 local communities covered. 
E) 27.1% decrease recorded. 
F) 98 villages (Lake Urmia=77, Shadegan=10, and Bakhtegan=11).
G) 3 Communication, Education, Public Awareness (CEPA) centers which are established and functional (one center in each of Lake Urmia, Shadegan and Bakhtegan wetlands)
H) 2 wetlands are covered.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">A) 3 MPs action plan developed/revised and are under implementation (1 action plan for each site)
B) At least 400,000 ha of fragile wetland ecosystems under the coverage of customized management plans (under implementation) (250,000 ha Lake Urmia, 100,000 ha Shadegan, 50,000 ha Bakhtegan)
C) 3 monitoring stations equipped and operational (1 in each wetland)
D) 2,400 local communities benefited from livelihood initiatives (1600 person in Lake Urmia basin and 400 person in each of Shadegan and Bakhtegan, out of which 50% of them are women) 
E) 30% of decrease in water and agrochemical usage in selected pilot sites
F) 140 new pilot villages in which climate smart practices have been implemented (80 pilots in Lake Urmia basin and 30 for each of Shadegan and Bakhtegan wetlands)
G) 3 CEPA centers which are established and functional (one center in each of Lake Urmia, Shadegan and Bakhtegan wetlands)
H) 18 wetland management initiatives (biodiversity conservation, community mobilization, festivals, campaigns, fairs, etc) being implemented by local community (12 in Lake Urmia basin and 3 in each of Shadegan and Bakhtegan wetland.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
    </period>
